The relevant propositions are those that relate fruit disconnection to box disconnection: Prop 1‑6 and Prop 5 in particular.  
Box two is disconnected from box three. From Prop 5 we can infer that the fruit covered by box two (the medium green apple) is disconnected from the fruit covered by box three (the medium yellow apple). However, there is no proposition that makes a fruit inside one box (the medium yellow apple in box two) disconnected from a fruit covered by a different, disconnected box. Consequently we cannot conclude that the medium yellow apple inside box two is disconnected from any fruit. Since at least one medium yellow apple (the one in box two) is not guaranteed to be disconnected from a fruit, the statement “all medium yellow apples are disconnected from a fruit” is false.

